The law texts in this repository come from four sources. Each commit names its source in its `Source:` trailer and,
for the texts added from 2026-11-26, in its `Source-status:` trailer.

legislation.gov.uk (The National Archives): the Constitution of Kiribati as made, taken from The Kiribati Independence
Order 1979 (SI 1979/719) (https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/1979/719/made). Contains public sector information
licensed under the Open Government Licence v3.0
(https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/).

Office of Te Beretitenti (https://www.president.gov.ki/resources/gazettes-instruments.html): the texts marked
"official (Office of Te Beretitenti, ...)" are the Government of Kiribati's own published copies. They are official
texts of the law; no terms of use are published with them.

FAOLEX, the FAO legal database (https://faolex.fao.org/): the texts marked "secondary copy (FAOLEX, ...)" are
FAOLEX's copies. FAO terms (https://www.fao.org/contact-us/terms/): material may be copied, downloaded and printed
for private study, research and teaching purposes, or for use in non-commercial products or services, provided
that FAO is acknowledged as the source. Source credit: FAOLEX, Food and Agriculture Organization of the United
Nations.

WIPO Lex (https://www.wipo.int/wipolex/): the texts marked "secondary copy (WIPO Lex, ...)" are WIPO Lex's copies
of national laws, provided free of charge by WIPO. WIPO's terms (https://www.wipo.int/tools/en/disclaim.html): its
online content is issued under CC BY 4.0 except where more restrictive terms are stated. Source credit: WIPO Lex,
World Intellectual Property Organization.

Constitute (https://www.constituteproject.org/, CC BY-NC 3.0) was read as a cross-check only; no text is taken from
it. PacLII is not used.

The laws themselves are Kiribati's. This repository is public, free and non-commercial, and keeps each text as its
source gives it.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
